From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vipul Cariappa <vipulcariappa@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 18:51:27 +0530
Subject: Ship only the C++23 and C23 kernels in the wasm build

Every kernelspec in a JupyterLite site points at its own copy of the kernel, and
this one is a whole clang: shipping standards nobody selected costs a visitor
tens of megabytes each. The two newest are enough for a deployment.

The families dropped here could not work in a browser regardless. The CUDA
kernels have no device and no CUDA toolkit in the emscripten sysroot for the
host pass to include, and their wasm kernelspecs were copies of the plain C++
ones, so the launcher showed two identical entries per standard. OpenMP has no
libomp built for wasm32-emscripten: with -fopenmp the incremental module fails
to load, and without it clang ignores the pragma and the loop runs on one
thread while looking like it worked.

Native builds keep every kernel they had.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index b7ac66e..b7e77d1 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -174,16 +174,28 @@ function(configure_kernel kernel)
 endfunction()
 
 message("Configure kernels: ...")
-configure_kernel("/share/jupyter/kernels/xcpp17/")
-configure_kernel("/share/jupyter/kernels/xcpp20/")
-configure_kernel("/share/jupyter/kernels/xcpp23/")
-configure_kernel("/share/jupyter/kernels/xcpp17-cuda/")
-configure_kernel("/share/jupyter/kernels/xcpp20-cuda/")
-configure_kernel("/share/jupyter/kernels/xcpp23-cuda/")
-configure_kernel("/share/jupyter/kernels/xc11/")
-configure_kernel("/share/jupyter/kernels/xc17/")
-configure_kernel("/share/jupyter/kernels/xc23/")
-if(NOT EMSCRIPTEN)
+if(EMSCRIPTEN)
+  # A wasm deployment ships the two newest standards and nothing else. Every
+  # kernel here is a separate copy of the whole clang-based kernel in the site,
+  # so an unused one is tens of megabytes a visitor may have to fetch.
+  #
+  # The families that are left out cannot work in a browser anyway: the CUDA
+  # kernels have no device and no CUDA toolkit in the emscripten sysroot, and
+  # the OpenMP ones have no libomp built for wasm32-emscripten -- with -fopenmp
+  # the incremental module fails to load, and without it the pragma is ignored
+  # and the loop silently runs on one thread.
+  configure_kernel("/share/jupyter/kernels/xcpp23/")
+  configure_kernel("/share/jupyter/kernels/xc23/")
+else()
+  configure_kernel("/share/jupyter/kernels/xcpp17/")
+  configure_kernel("/share/jupyter/kernels/xcpp20/")
+  configure_kernel("/share/jupyter/kernels/xcpp23/")
+  configure_kernel("/share/jupyter/kernels/xcpp17-cuda/")
+  configure_kernel("/share/jupyter/kernels/xcpp20-cuda/")
+  configure_kernel("/share/jupyter/kernels/xcpp23-cuda/")
+  configure_kernel("/share/jupyter/kernels/xc11/")
+  configure_kernel("/share/jupyter/kernels/xc17/")
+  configure_kernel("/share/jupyter/kernels/xc23/")
   configure_kernel("/share/jupyter/kernels/xcpp23-omp/")
   configure_kernel("/share/jupyter/kernels/xc23-omp/")
 endif()
